  "dom_id": "step-q343202",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14212968/assets/305398b239bbc784fb5e5a1ec7ef2020a19a033dcda150e84f9c4a2a72a96adf.png)\n\nA lifeguard $L$ is watching a weather balloon $W$ rise vertically from a point $S$ on the beach. The point $S$ is $10\\,\\text{m}$ away from the lifeguard. If the balloon is rising at a constant speed of $1\\,\\text{m/s},$ determine the rate at which the angle of elevation $\\theta $ formed by the lifeguard and the balloon is increasing at the moment when $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe angle of elevation is increasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{rad/s}.$",
